{"kind":"event","event_id":8470,"event_uid":"01M2Q0XHBA10ZCAJR0DRV69YF2","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":351,"issue_uid":"01M2Q0SYN3NW4KM9DVE80CFFFN","issue_short_id":"fffn","actor":"impl:2@run-173","hlc_physical_ms":1789626598762,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"70b7b41dbf6224d0c0c05b99d37fac7d829a51d6cea22ec59e97716af6d72d0f","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q0XHB9MRTQS8JPX3ZFKJWC","author":"impl:2@run-173","body":"Approach for task 2 (memory sized by browser concurrency):\n\n1. `fleet/launch.mjs`: add exported `browsersFor(compiled)` reading `compiled.waves` (task-object form) and counting, per wave, tasks whose `proofTests` carries a path under `tests/state-exams/`; return the largest such count, 0 when there is no waves array or the entries are id strings.\n2. Extend `vmSizeFor(widestWave, cap, browsers)`: cpu unchanged; memory `min(cap, 2 + W)GB` when browsers is 0/omitted, `min(cap, max(6, ceil(2 + 1.25 x browsers)))GB` when browsers >= 1.\n3. Lift the `sizeFromCompile` closure out of `launch()` into a pure top-level export `sizeFromCompile(compiled, { cpuCap, memoryCap, cpu, memory })` returning `{ width, browsers, cpu, memory }`; call it from `launch()` at both sites with the compiled object and the four options.\n4. `stampWidth` note gains `browsers=<C>`; the launch result literal gains `browsers,` between `memory,` and `width,`.\n5. RUNBOOK capacity item 2, first-run `## capacity`, and CONTRACT's launch-order bullet gain the browsers rule and the 12GB ceiling recommendation.\n\nThe two existing launcher sims are left untouched (their fixtures name no state exam, so `2 + W` still holds by M2's first clause).","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:29:58.761081896Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T06:29:58.762Z"}
